This could be fixed by a change, admittedly a difficult one, to seperate 
  Nethack cleanly into client and server modules, each capable of 
running on seperate processes on seperate machines, communicating over 
an IP socket. This would allow anyone to connect to NAO from the client 
of their choice: ASCII, tile, Falcon's Eye, etc. It would also allow 
correct logging and playback from any client and provide easier hooks 
for people that want to experiment with Nethack bots.

Admittedly none of these are core concerns for most NH players but they 
have all been discussed previously in this group.


